Per-cell coverage stays qualified with fixture evidence (issue #507).

Four required cells gate their own combined LCOV
report separately through coverage_bin against their versioned
inventory: seed linux_x86_64 plus linux_arm64 native (issue #410) plus
macos arm64 native (issue
#412)
plus windows x86_64 MSVC-compatible native (issue #414). Same
first-party scope in every cell; only the inventory path differs.
No cross-cell union, no averaged percentages, no rounding up.

Accepted decision: 100% non-ignored lines in this repo via the seed
exact gate (zero uncovered lines in tools/coverage/seed-inventory.txt
scope), configurable --min-coverage requirement for users per-cell.
Codecov stays opt-in only, never required. Cells, languages, and
metrics stay separate with no cross-cell union.

Starlark keeps the evidence-backed behavioral fallback: genuine
executable-line instrumentation is infeasible under the pinned Bazel
(9.2.0), proven by the 0-byte coverage.dat probe with zero SF records
and the never-accepted upstream proposal (bazelbuild/bazel#15594).
The checked behavioral matrix (matrix_validation) is repository
metadata, never presented as source-line or branch coverage and never
combined into a source-coverage percentage.

Seed only for platform plus consumer plus release evidence; no
Supported claim. Floors stay owned under issue #500, LCOV accounting
stays owned under issue #501.
